LBL_HOTEND_TEMPERATURE=Hotend temperature:
LBL_ID_PINS=ID pins:
LBL_IMPACTS_DETECTED_SESSION=Impacts detected this session:
HELP_AOI_RING_IGNORED=In AOI Inspection mode, ring on/off here is ignored - use that tool's own ring mode control instead (0x150 covers on/off/strobe there). Color still applies.
LBL_INTERLOCK_ARMED=Interlock armed (required for any power > 0 to matter)
HELP_INTERLOCK_MUST_BE_ARMED=Interlock must be explicitly armed below - this is a real laser.
LBL_LAST_IMPACT=Last impact:
LBL_LAYER_FAN_RPM=Layer fan RPM:
LBL_LAYER_FAN_POWER=Layer fan power (0-255):
LBL_LIVE_TEMPERATURE=Live temperature:
TITLE_LOG=Log
BTN_MOVE_EXTRUDER_ONCE=Move extruder once
BTN_MOVE=Move
HELP_NO_WATCHDOG_STALL_DETECTOR=No communication watchdog on this fan - it's protected by a stall detector instead (0 RPM 3s after starting = Critical Error), since losing this fan matters even if the master goes briefly quiet.
STATUS_NO_RESPONSE_CHECK_WIRING=No response - check wiring/power/bitrate
STATUS_NO_RESPONSE_ANY_BITRATE=No response at any standard bitrate
STATUS_NO_RESPONSE_0X110=No response to 0x110 - is the firmware on this board recent enough to support it?
HELP_NO_WATCHDOG_HOLDS_VALUE=No watchdog on this command - it holds until a new value is sent, 0 speed engages the active brake.
STATUS_NOT_CONNECTED=Not connected
LBL_NOZZLE_SETPOINT=Nozzle setpoint (\u00b0C, 0-300):
LBL_OLED_MODE=OLED mode:
HELP_ONE_SHOT_NO_TELEMETRY=One-shot command, no telemetry from this tool - the firmware enables the driver on receiving this frame and cuts power once the move finishes.
BTN_OPEN_BUS_MONITOR=Open Raw Bus Monitor...
LBL_PART_DETECTED_LM393=Part detected (LM393):
BTN_PAUSE=Pause
LBL_PERSISTENCE_FRAM=Persistence F-RAM (FM24CL64B, shares I2C2 with the OLED):
LBL_POWER_0_255=Power (0-255):
BTN_QUERY_DIAG0=Query DIAG0
BTN_QUERY_STATE=Query State
BTN_QUERY=Query
HELP_READONLY_SET_VIA_FLASHER=Read-only here - set via URTC Flasher's CAN OTA section, since it's a one-time hardware-configuration step done alongside a firmware update, not something to change from this tool.
BTN_REFRESH=Refresh
LBL_REPEAT_EVERY=Repeat every
LBL_RESPONSE=Response:
LBL_RING_LED_RGB=Ring LED (R/G/B):
HELP_RING_COLOR_FROM_GLOBAL=Ring color comes from the Global Controls panel above (0x100) - this only controls on/off/strobe timing, not the color itself.
LBL_RING_MODE=Ring mode:
CHK_RING_ON=Ring on
BTN_RUN_SELF_TEST=Run Self-Test...
LBL_SPI_BYTES_TO_SEND=SPI bytes to send (hex, space-separated):
TITLE_SCAN_PROBE_TELEMETRY=Scan Probe - event telemetry only (0x095)
BTN_SEND_ONCE=Send Once
BTN_SEND=Send
HELP_SENDS_RAW_FRAME=Sends a raw frame - useful for a command that doesn't have its own control here yet, or for testing something not (or not yet) documented in CANBUS.TXT. No validation beyond ID range and DLC\u22648 - whatever this sends is exactly what goes on the bus.
HELP_SCAN_PROBE_INTERRUPT=Sent straight from the touch interrupt at the lowest (highest-priority) CAN ID on the whole bus, bypassing every scheduler - by design, this should arrive essentially instantly on contact, every time.
RADIO_SERIAL_SLCAN=Serial / SLCAN
LBL_SETPOINT_TEMPERATURE=Setpoint temperature (\u00b0C, 0-450):
HELP_SHOWS_EVERY_FRAME=Shows every frame seen, any ID - independent of the active tool panel.
RADIO_SOCKETCAN_NATIVE=SocketCAN (native)
LBL_SPEED_0_255=Speed (0-255):
LBL_STATUS_LED_OVERRIDE=Status LED override (R/G/B):
LBL_STEPS=Steps:
LBL_STROBE_PERIOD=Strobe period:
LBL_TOOL_NUMBER=Tool #:
TAB_TOOL_CONTROLS=Tool Controls
LBL_TRANSPORT=Transport:
STATUS_TRYING_EACH_BITRATE=Trying each bitrate...
HELP_UP_TO_7_BYTES_SPI=Up to 7 bytes per transfer (CS held low for the whole thing) - matches what a single 0x180 frame can carry (1 length byte + up to 7 data bytes).
TITLE_VACUUM_TELEMETRY=Vacuum Pickup - telemetry only (0x145)
LBL_MS_UNIT=ms
LBL_CAN_INTERFACE=CAN interface:
HELP_SOCKETCAN_BITRATE_OS_LEVEL=SocketCAN's bitrate is set at the OS level (ip link), not here
