TITLE_DEBUG_BUNDLE_SAVED=Debug bundle saved
MSG_SAVED_TO=Saved to:\n{path}
TITLE_CONNECTION_FAILED_PERMISSION=Connection failed - permission denied
MSG_PERMISSION_DENIED_HELP={msg}\n\nOn Linux, serial devices usually need your user in the 'dialout' group:\n\n    sudo usermod -a -G dialout $USER\n\nThen log out and back in (group membership is read at login) and try again.
TITLE_PYSERIAL_NOT_INSTALLED=pyserial not installed
MSG_PYSERIAL_NEEDED_AUTODETECT=Auto-detect needs pyserial for serial/SLCAN connections.\n\nInstall it with: pip install pyserial
TITLE_RUN_SELF_TEST_Q=Run self-test?
MSG_SELF_TEST_CONFIRM=This sends a small number of safe, at-rest commands (setpoint/speed/power all 0) to verify the board responds as expected for its detected tool - nothing here heats, fires, or spins anything at meaningful power. Continue?
TITLE_ERASE_FRAM_Q=Erase F-RAM?
MSG_ERASE_FRAM_CONFIRM=This permanently erases the saved parameter state on the board's persistence F-RAM. This cannot be undone. Continue?
TITLE_PLAIN_STEPPER_MOTION={tool} - plain stepper motion (0x120)
